<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan State Oil up 3.99 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan State Oil up 3.99 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blue-chip Pakistan State Oil rose 13.0 rupees, or 3.99 percent, to 339 on Wednesday after the government announced a 7.86 percent rupee devaluation and raised petroleum prices 10 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>A turnover of 11,700 shares of the stock was recorded in early trade.</p>
<p>&quot;Devaluation of rupee and rise in petroleum prices are good for the earnings of the company,&quot; dealer Ather Raouf said. &quot;It is a good scrip and will gain further.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
